{
 "theme": "crypt",
 "about": "Stone crypts (the game's forest and sunken crypts, joined by type \"\"): grey stone walls, arches and pillars, torches, bones and roots, iron gates. Human scale: rooms on a 2-4 m grid, doorways 2-3 m.",
 "made_by": "tools/dungeons/palette_tool.py (curation in CURATED there; everything else read from the game's files)",
 "fields": {
  "role": "what it's for; structural roles (arch, block, ceiling, door, floor, gate, pillar, platform, rail, ramp, stair, wall) must be solid",
  "mount": "ground: stands on a floor (prop_check.py); hang: needs something right above its origin or a chain on its top; wall: against a wall; span: rests on two supports; structure: what others stand on; free: anywhere",
  "scale": "[min, max] that looks right and stays solid; stairs keep 1 (step height)",
  "tier": "the land it looks like it belongs to (1 Meadows .. 8 Deep North): a look hint, not gameplay (enemies and loot follow the entrance's biome)",
  "size/min/max/origin": "its shape's box in its own frame (m); origin: where its origin sits on that box (foot, top, centre...)",
  "solid": "a character bumps into it in our rooms (the game's collision matrix; items fixed by BuildSolid.cs)",
  "lights": "range, intensity, colour; lit: shines once stripped (a Fireplace's burning objects are switched on); lod: fades with distance",
  "gives": "what the game would make it give or do: stripped as scenery; a networked prefab (networked) may be a Saved part instead",
  "height": "its height at scale 1 (m)",
  "climb": "ledges: its footholds (faces a player can stand on, no steeper than 38 degrees, with at least 0.1 m2 of them seen from above in a 0.2 m height band) as height ranges above its foot at scale 1, upright as the prefab stands; top: the highest reachable from the floor, each within a jump (1.6 m: gravity 20, jump force 8, Jump skill 0) of the last; top_skilled: the same with Jump skill 100 (3.14 m); 0: none. Scale the ledges by the part's y scale; a part turned off upright exposes other faces (treat a smooth bar or column as only its top end)",
  "upright": "flat (thin along y: a floor tile, stand it up for a wall), upright (thin along x or z: a wall piece, use as it is), block",
  "safe": "fine as stripped scenery; saved_only: works only as a Saved part (chests, pickables, spawners)",
  "by_role": "{role: [default, variants...]}: the roles below without their notes",
  "sets": "the dressing sets it suits (giant: ossuary, ruin, forge, archive, engine, armoury; Dvergr: store, workshop, tavern, barracks)",
  "max_span": "a panel's longest side (m) before its stretched texture smears",
  "roles": "the same pieces by a theme recipe's roles (first = default, others = variants), with how each role's pieces are placed",
  "render": "a picture in the mesh cache (C:\\Users\\DHack\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\quaddungeon_meshes); the theme's contact sheet is palettes/crypt_sheet.png there"
 },
